er membrane and facilitates the movement of preproteins into the TOM40 translocation pore (PubMed:18331822). The TOM complex associates with the ion channel VDAC2 and PINK1 kinase at depolarized mitochondria, this interaction stabilizes PINK1 at the outer mitochondrial membrane and triggers downstream mitophagy by the recruitment of the E3 ubiquitin ligase PRKN (PubMed:40080546). Required for the translocation across the mitochondrial outer membrane of cytochrome P450 monooxygenases (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}